FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied:
- Hold DYNAMIC_PROC_INFO -> FILETABLE.inner -> FILETABLE.fd -> ALLOCATOR -> SIGACTIONS_LOCK across the file-table copy and address-space clone in fork_inner using pre-reserved upper slots, with a single AtomicPtr allocator-hook struct, RAII parent release on every path, and shared child unlock in child_hook_common before closing cur_filetable_fd.
- Reconcile the child's userspace file table against kernel FileTableVerb::Refresh (after lseek(0, SEEK_SET)) in child_hook_common, closing kernel-only slots except handed-over fork handles, dropping table-only phantoms, and preserving flags on surviving descriptors.
- Ensure exec'd and spawned programs never receive close-on-exec descriptors: hold FILETABLE.inner -> FILETABLE.fd across dup("copy") and listing in posix_spawn, track file_actions, clone new_file_table after closing close-on-exec descriptors while keeping ExtraInfo handles, fall back to per-descriptor close accepting EBADF only in both fexec_impl and posix_spawn, and terminate/reap the child via bounded ChildCleanupGuard on spawn failure.
- Consume new_filetable_weak_fd with take() after CallFlags::FD move in fork_inner, release image_file before FdGuard::to_upper() in execve so each descriptor has one owner on both success and error paths, and set O_CLOEXEC atomically on pipe2's write end.

